    "id": "train-7300",
    "question": "John's neighbor tells him to walk his dog for 1 hour each day for a total of $10. He does this for April, save for the 4 Sundays in April. He later spent $50 on books and gave his sister Kaylee the same amount. How much money did John have left?",
    "gold": "160",
    "answer": "April has 30 days, so if he didn't walk the dog on Sundays, he worked for a total of 30 days - 4 days = <<30-4=26>>26 days.\nIf each day he earned $10, he ends up with 26 days * $10/day = $<<26*10=260>>260 .\nAfter buying books and giving his sister $50, he ends up with $260 - $50 - $50 = $<<260-50-50=160>>160\n#### 160"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much money John has left, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of days in April.\n2. Determine the number of days John walked the dog.\n3. Calculate the total amount of money John earned from walking the dog.\n4. Subtract the amount spent on books and the amount given to his sister from the total money earned.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total number of days in April. April has 30 days.\n\nNext, we need to determine the number of days John walked the dog. Since John did not walk the dog on 4 Sundays, he walked the dog on:\n\\[ 30 - 4 = 26 \\text{ days} \\]\n\nJohn earns $10 for each day he walks the dog. Therefore, the total amount of money John earned is:\n\\[ 26 \\times 10 = 260 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nJohn spent $50 on books and gave his sister Kaylee $50. So, the total amount of money he spent is:\n\\[ 50 + 50 = 100 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nTo find out how much money John has left, we subtract the amount he spent from the total amount he earned:\n\\[ 260 - 100 = 160 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThus, the amount of money John has left is:\n\\[ \\boxed{160} \\]",
